# Design <-> Token discrepancies

Use a dedicated section to track mismatches between Figma design intent and token usage.

## Section name and placement

- Section title: `## Design–Token Discrepancies`
- Component docs: place after `## Related Components` and before `## Gaps / TBD` (see `component-doc-structure.mdc`).
- If no discrepancies exist, omit the section entirely.

## Required table format

Use this exact table schema:

| Discrepancy | Impact | Pending action | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |

### Field guidance

- `Discrepancy`: factual mismatch (hardcoded value, missing token, naming mismatch, unmapped variant).
- `Impact`: short impact statement on consistency/usability/maintenance.
- `Pending action`: concrete remediation task.
- `Status`: `open`, `accepted`, or `resolved`.

## Content rules

- Record only verifiable mismatches.
- Do not invent root causes.
- If evidence is incomplete, mark the row with `TBD` in the relevant cell.
